[h1] Grid

[p-]
The grid tag lays elements out in horizontal columns. Children fill
columns left to right, then wrap to the next row automatically.
Any tag that works on a normal page works inside a grid.
[-p]

[h2] Basic usage

[p] Open and close with [grid-] and [-grid]. The columns= attribute is required:

[code-]
[grid- columns=auto;auto]

[p] Left column
[p] Right column

[-grid]
[-code]

[grid- columns=auto;auto]

[p] Left column
[p] Right column

[-grid]

[h2] columns

[p-]
Each value in columns= defines one column. Values can be a fixed pixel
width (e.g. 100) or auto. Auto columns share whatever space is left after
fixed columns are measured.
[-p]

[p] Two equal columns:

[code-]
[grid- columns=auto;auto]

[p] Column one
[p] Column two

[-grid]
[-code]

[grid- columns=auto;auto]

[p] Column one
[p] Column two

[-grid]

[p] Three columns — one fixed, two auto:

[code-]
[grid- columns=120;auto;auto]

[p] Fixed 120px
[p] Auto fills rest
[p] Auto fills rest

[-grid]
[-code]

[grid- columns=120;auto;auto]

[p] Fixed 120px
[p] Auto fills rest
[p] Auto fills rest

[-grid]

[p] Rows wrap automatically — every N children start a new row:

[code-]
[grid- columns=auto;auto;auto]

[p] Name
[p] Date
[p] Score

[p] saturn91
[p] 01/01/1970
[p] 9001

[p] John Doe
[p] 15/03/1985
[p] 42

[-grid]
[-code]

[grid- columns=auto;auto;auto]

[p] Name
[p] Date
[p] Score

[p] saturn91
[p] 01/01/1970
[p] 9001

[p] John Doe
[p] 15/03/1985
[p] 42

[-grid]

[h2] gap

[p-]
The default column gap is 4px and the default row gap is 0px. Use gap=
to override both at once.
[-p]

[code-]
[grid- columns=auto;auto gap=16]

[p] Wide gap between columns
[p] and between rows too

[p] Second row left
[p] Second row right

[-grid]
[-code]

[grid- columns=auto;auto gap=16]

[p] Wide gap between columns
[p] and between rows too

[p] Second row left
[p] Second row right

[-grid]

[p] Set gap=0 to remove all spacing:

[code-]
[grid- columns=auto;auto;auto gap=0]

[p] Flush
[p] Side
[p] By side

[-grid]
[-code]

[grid- columns=auto;auto;auto gap=0]

[p] Flush
[p] Side
[p] By side

[-grid]

[h2] gapX and gapY

[p-]
Use gapX= to control only the column gap and gapY= to control only the
row gap. Both override gap= when present.
[-p]

[code-]
[grid- columns=auto;auto gapX=20 gapY=0]

[p] Wide column gap
[p] no row gap

[p] Row two left
[p] Row two right

[-grid]
[-code]

[grid- columns=auto;auto gapX=20 gapY=0]

[p] Wide column gap
[p] no row gap

[p] Row two left
[p] Row two right

[-grid]

[code-]
[grid- columns=auto;auto gapX=0 gapY=12]

[p] No column gap
[p] row gap of 12px

[p] Row two left
[p] Row two right

[-grid]
[-code]

[grid- columns=auto;auto gapX=0 gapY=12]

[p] No column gap
[p] row gap of 12px

[p] Row two left
[p] Row two right

[-grid]

[h2] Text alignment inside columns

[p] Children inside a grid accept the same align= values as everywhere else:

[code-]
[grid- columns=auto;auto;auto]

[p align=left] Left
[p align=center] Center
[p align=right] Right

[-grid]
[-code]

[grid- columns=auto;auto;auto]

[p align=left] Left
[p align=center] Center
[p align=right] Right

[-grid]

[p] Headings respect alignment too:

[code-]
[grid- columns=auto;auto;auto]

[h2 align=left] Left
[h2 align=center] Center
[h2 align=right] Right

[-grid]
[-code]

[grid- columns=auto;auto;auto]

[h2 align=left] Left
[h2 align=center] Center
[h2 align=right] Right

[-grid]

[h2] Links in columns

[p] Grid columns are great for building nav bars. Use align=center to center each link:

[code-]
[grid- columns=auto;auto;auto;auto gapX=0]

[link file=index.podweb align=center] Home
[link file=how-to.podweb align=center] Tutorial
[link file=about.podweb align=center] About
[link file=roadmap.podweb align=center] Roadmap

[-grid]
[-code]

[grid- columns=auto;auto;auto;auto gapX=0]

[link file=index.podweb align=center] Home
[link file=how-to.podweb align=center] Tutorial
[link file=about.podweb align=center] About
[link file=roadmap.podweb align=center] Roadmap

[-grid]

[h2] Images in columns

[p] Images respect align= and scale down to fit their column:

[code-]
[grid- columns=auto;auto]

[img url=podnet://48932/banner.gfx align=center]
[img url=podnet://48932/banner_squibble.gfx align=center]

[-grid]
[-code]

[grid- columns=auto;auto]

[img url=podnet://48932/banner.gfx align=center]
[img url=podnet://48932/banner_squibble.gfx align=center]

[-grid]

[h2] Sidebar layout

[p] Combine a fixed image column with an auto text column for a sidebar:

[code-]
[grid- columns=80;auto gap=6]

[img url=podnet://48932/banner.gfx align=left]

[p-]
This text sits beside the image. The image
column is fixed at 80px and the text fills
the remaining space automatically.
[-p]

[-grid]
[-code]

[grid- columns=80;auto gap=6]

[img url=podnet://48932/banner.gfx align=left]

[p-]
This text sits beside the image. The image
column is fixed at 80px and the text fills
the remaining space automatically.
[-p]

[-grid]

[h2] Supported tags inside grid

[p-]
All standard tags work inside a grid column. Each child element fills
one cell. The row height is always the tallest cell in that row.
[-p]

[code-]
h1  h2  h3        headings — alignment respected
p   p-            paragraphs — inline links, align, font, color all work
link              standalone links — align, color, hover_color all work
img               images — align and resize respected, scaled to column width
download          download links — same as standalone
code  code-       code blocks — fill the column width
break             vertical spacer
[-code]

[p-]
Comments and webrings are full-width elements and are not intended
for use inside grid columns.
[-p]

